{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: no data fields were added or changed. The model-block priors were rewritten from `to_vector(alpha)` and `to_vector(beta)` to top-level parameter sampling statements and placed before any parameter-dependent likelihood computation. The indexed likelihood loop `y[n] ~ categorical_logit(...)` was replaced by the single built-in vectorized statement `y ~ categorical_logit_glm(tanh(x * alpha), rep_vector(0, K), beta)`, which uses the same logits as the original `rbm(x, alpha, beta)`. `yt` is context data used only in generated quantities and is not protected.
","model_safe_stan":"functions {
  /**
   * Returns linear predictor for restricted Boltzman machine (RBM).
   * Assumes one-hidden layer with logistic sigmoid activation.
   *
   * @param x Predictors (N x M)
   * @param alpha First-layer weights (M x J)
   * @param beta Second-layer weights (J x (K - 1))
   * @return Linear predictor for output layer of RBM.
   */
  matrix rbm(matrix x, matrix alpha, matrix beta) {
    return tanh(x * alpha) * beta;
  }
}
data {
  int<lower=0> N; // num train instances
  int<lower=0> M; // num train predictors
  matrix[N, M] x; // train predictors
  int<lower=2> K; // num categories
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=K> y; // train category

  int<lower=1> J; // num hidden units

  int<lower=0> Nt; // num test instances
  matrix[Nt, M] xt; // test predictors
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=K> yt; // test category
}
parameters {
  matrix[M, J] alpha;
  matrix[J, K] beta;
}
model {
  // priors
  alpha ~ normal(0, 2);
  beta ~ normal(0, 2);

  // likelihood
  y ~ categorical_logit_glm(tanh(x * alpha), rep_vector(0, K), beta);
}
generated quantities {
  array[Nt] int<lower=1, upper=K> yt_sim; // test observations
  real log_p_yt;
  real accuracy;
  matrix[K, Nt] v;

  v = rbm(xt, alpha, beta)';
  log_p_yt = 0;
  accuracy = 0;
  for (n in 1 : Nt) {
    vector[K] theta;
    theta = softmax(col(v, n));
    log_p_yt = log_p_yt + categorical_lpmf(yt_sim | theta);
    yt_sim[n] = categorical_rng(theta);
    if (yt_sim[n] == yt[n]) {
      accuracy = accuracy + 1;
    }
  }
  accuracy = accuracy / Nt;
}
